WEBVTT

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.875
There is a legend of an imperial son
that has been told on the Planet Jurai.

00:01:42.582 --> 00:01:45.419
He was the best swordsman
ever seen and gifted

00:01:45.419 --> 00:01:47.478
with unmatched mastery of Jurai's power.

00:02:02.502 --> 00:02:05.639
He was compassionate and affectionate.

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:07.539
Everybody adored him.

00:02:11.978 --> 00:02:19.319
But he simply vanished without a
trace before ascending to the throne.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:23.457
Since then, it's been unknown where he went.

00:02:23.457 --> 00:02:26.026
His name was Yosho.

00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:30.224
This is the legend of a crown prince handed
down for generations on the Planet Jurai.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.676
Ahh, you know, I think there's nothing
quite like some quality time with family.

00:02:42.676 --> 00:02:44.144
You're right. It is the best.

00:02:44.144 --> 00:02:47.814
If we're all family, Tenchi
and I are husband and wife, huh?

00:02:47.814 --> 00:02:49.748
No, of course not!

00:02:51.952 --> 00:02:53.753
Hey, this is not a sitcom!

00:02:53.753 --> 00:02:56.356
We have more important
stuff to think about, don't we?

00:02:56.356 --> 00:02:57.824
Just calm down.

00:02:57.824 --> 00:02:58.925
But...

00:02:58.925 --> 00:03:00.460
Look there, Tenchi.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.430
That supernova is just gorgeous, isn't it?

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.464
Oh, yeah.

00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:06.032
It is beautiful.

00:03:06.032 --> 00:03:09.503
I can't calm down when outside our
window there is nothing but space!

00:03:09.503 --> 00:03:10.403
You should be thankful to Washu.

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:13.673
We only have our house because she fixed it.

00:03:13.673 --> 00:03:17.110
Well, it was simply compressed
down to a portable size.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.912
Fixing it was easy... just like
making a frozen dinner.

00:03:18.912 --> 00:03:22.282
Lucky it was just the perfect
size for Yagami's cargo bay.

00:03:22.282 --> 00:03:26.082
Thanks to Washu, we have
enough bedding for everyone.

00:03:27.921 --> 00:03:30.991
Hi, there, Kiyone. I brought you some tea.

00:03:30.991 --> 00:03:32.481
Thank you.

00:03:35.195 --> 00:03:38.995
Somehow that view just
doesn't help me relax, not at all.

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:43.637
How are you guys feeling? Any better?

00:03:43.637 --> 00:03:47.908
Ah, my energy circuit is
not yet completely recharged.

00:03:47.908 --> 00:03:50.677
I transformed you back into normal size.

00:03:50.677 --> 00:03:52.946
You could show me
some gratitude, you know.

00:03:52.946 --> 00:03:55.815
We would all be better off, if they
had remained in their compact size.

00:03:55.815 --> 00:03:58.318
I think they take up too much space.

00:03:58.318 --> 00:03:59.886
I would not like that.

00:03:59.886 --> 00:04:02.081
Being condensed once was enough.

00:04:04.057 --> 00:04:07.083
Attention, everybody.
Report to the bridge at once!

00:04:08.862 --> 00:04:10.397
That's strange.

00:04:10.397 --> 00:04:12.165
Can anybody hear me?

00:04:12.165 --> 00:04:14.301
I need everyone up on the bridge.

00:04:14.301 --> 00:04:16.235
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:04:18.572 --> 00:04:20.607
I wonder what's going on.

00:04:20.607 --> 00:04:22.342
Yeah.

00:04:22.342 --> 00:04:24.244
Mihoshi, answer me!

00:04:24.244 --> 00:04:26.474
Hey! Anybody home?!

00:04:28.248 --> 00:04:30.016
<i>Tonight's the night that</i>

00:04:30.016 --> 00:04:31.851
<i>I'm gonna have my desire</i>

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:36.189
<i>Most people think I'm aloof</i>

00:04:36.189 --> 00:04:42.929
<i>Because I'm such a beauty</i>

00:04:42.929 --> 00:04:46.533
<i>Don't worry about it, only for you</i>

00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:50.303
<i>Heaven's given you a chance</i>

00:04:50.303 --> 00:04:54.074
<i>I can reserve the honeymoon suite</i>

00:04:54.074 --> 00:04:57.744
<i>at the sweetest hotel</i>

00:04:57.744 --> 00:05:03.316
<i>Don't worry about catching the last train</i>

00:05:03.316 --> 00:05:09.389
<i>Don't you know it's Christmas time?</i>

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:12.659
<i>Come on, baby, we
can do whatever we like</i>

00:05:12.659 --> 00:05:20.433
<i>We can party all through the night</i>

00:05:20.433 --> 00:05:23.937
<i>It'll be our celebration</i>

00:05:23.937 --> 00:05:27.073
<i>Don't be a square</i>

00:05:27.073 --> 00:05:33.813
<i>The liquor store is still open now</i>

00:05:33.813 --> 00:05:36.149
Hello! What are you doing?!

00:05:36.149 --> 00:05:39.448
Can't you hear me?! Hello!

00:05:40.887 --> 00:05:44.015
What the hell are they doing?

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:51.898
<i>Oh, I am the only one</i>

00:05:51.898 --> 00:05:57.937
<i>You've never known someone like me</i>

00:05:57.937 --> 00:06:04.644
<i>So witty and so beautiful</i>

00:06:04.644 --> 00:06:10.450
<i>Yes, I'm the only one</i>

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:16.523
<i>Just try to find a fault with me</i>

00:06:16.523 --> 00:06:25.454
<i>It's like looking for a needle in a haystack</i>

00:06:29.335 --> 00:06:33.673
<i>And I can't even say</i>

00:06:33.673 --> 00:06:39.111
<i>The half of what I want to say</i>

00:06:41.047 --> 00:06:50.422
<i>Because I am so modest</i>

00:06:53.693 --> 00:07:00.100
<i>So now I say to you</i>

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:06.239
<i>You 700-year-old mummy woman</i>

00:07:06.239 --> 00:07:14.112
<i>I envy your incredible bluntness</i>

00:07:16.049 --> 00:07:17.744
What are you guys doing?!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.255
What?! Out of fuel?

00:07:22.255 --> 00:07:26.726
Eeh! Right. Yagami is running out of fuel.

00:07:26.726 --> 00:07:29.863
So why don't we just find a gas station?

00:07:29.863 --> 00:07:32.665
I wouldn't be calling a
meeting, if we could afford that.

00:07:32.665 --> 00:07:35.235
Some criminals we are.

00:07:35.235 --> 00:07:38.404
Nobody brought any money with them, huh?

00:07:38.404 --> 00:07:41.574
Now wait just a minute. I thought
we had some petty cash with us.

00:07:41.574 --> 00:07:45.066
Yeah, we spent it on that, didn't we?

00:07:48.081 --> 00:07:51.885
Oh! You mean we have a
critically important mission,

00:07:51.885 --> 00:07:53.486
to uncover a conspiracy on Planet Jurai,

00:07:53.486 --> 00:07:57.090
and we spent our money
on a karaoke machine?

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:00.393
Yeah. I wanna know who
bought that stupid thing anyway.

00:08:00.393 --> 00:08:01.895
It was you, Ryoko!

00:08:01.895 --> 00:08:03.692
Howdja know?

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.032
Can't you keep in mind our primary concern?

00:08:06.032 --> 00:08:09.969
You were getting into singing with
that machine like everyone else, though.

00:08:09.969 --> 00:08:12.639
The bottom line is that we have
to earn some money as we go.

00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:16.109
Otherwise we'll never make it to Planet Jurai.

00:08:16.109 --> 00:08:19.567
You're telling me I have to
get a job, while I'm on this trip?

00:08:24.184 --> 00:08:28.555
Princess Ayeka and her group are still at large.

00:08:28.555 --> 00:08:32.025
Police say the suspects may
have stopped at Planet Concor

00:08:32.025 --> 00:08:34.928
and are doing their best to search for
the criminals in the surrounding area.

00:08:34.928 --> 00:08:40.667
Police are also investigating
any possible reasons for this detour.

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:42.362
Let's go, Ken-Ohki.

00:08:48.274 --> 00:08:53.109
Ryoko, I won't let anybody else catch you.

00:09:04.357 --> 00:09:08.695
From headquarters to all patrol ships.

00:09:08.695 --> 00:09:13.066
Princess Ayeka and her
group are still at large.

00:09:13.066 --> 00:09:15.899
Please remain on full alert.

00:09:18.271 --> 00:09:21.074
Come on in. Stop by and have a drink.

00:09:21.074 --> 00:09:25.411
We're offering special prices
during our grand opening.

00:09:25.411 --> 00:09:28.815
Very low prices for a great time
with drinks and karaoke sing-along.

00:09:28.815 --> 00:09:30.617
Excuse me, mister.

00:09:30.617 --> 00:09:31.885
Please come on in.

00:09:31.885 --> 00:09:35.688
- Ah, I'm not... Uh...
- Don't be shy. Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:09:35.688 --> 00:09:38.816
Seat this customer, please.

00:09:39.759 --> 00:09:41.294
Welcome to our pub.

00:09:41.294 --> 00:09:43.057
How are you doing today?

00:09:43.563 --> 00:09:46.633
Please, follow me. Right this way, Sir.

00:09:46.633 --> 00:09:49.435
Ah, wait. Wait a minute. I wasn't gonna...

00:09:49.435 --> 00:09:50.203
Whoa!

00:09:50.203 --> 00:09:51.604
The hostess will be right with you.

00:09:51.604 --> 00:09:53.072
Uh, ah...

00:09:53.072 --> 00:09:55.308
Hi. How are you this evening?

00:09:55.308 --> 00:09:57.477
I am the owner of this pub.

00:09:57.477 --> 00:09:59.178
Nice to meet ya.

00:09:59.178 --> 00:10:02.815
We have a lot of pretty girls at this pub.

00:10:02.815 --> 00:10:04.784
What kind of girl would you like?

00:10:04.784 --> 00:10:07.587
Listen, I was just passing by.
I don't really want...

00:10:07.587 --> 00:10:13.693
Oh, really? You like a quiet and obedient type.

00:10:13.693 --> 00:10:16.596
Oh, Ryoko, will you
attend table five, please?

00:10:16.596 --> 00:10:18.364
Yes!

00:10:18.364 --> 00:10:19.666
You know, I am counting on you.

00:10:19.666 --> 00:10:22.302
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

00:10:22.302 --> 00:10:23.536
How are you doing?

00:10:23.536 --> 00:10:24.971
Huh? Well, I... ah...

00:10:24.971 --> 00:10:27.701
We have another customer!

00:10:36.015 --> 00:10:39.143
Come on! Drink up! Oh, yeah.

00:10:41.621 --> 00:10:44.824
Hey, we need some more drinks around here!

00:10:44.824 --> 00:10:46.392
H-Hey...

00:10:46.392 --> 00:10:49.595
And here are the drinks you ordered.

00:10:49.595 --> 00:10:51.358
Now you're talking.

00:10:52.699 --> 00:10:55.301
And here's the scotch and water you ordered.

00:10:55.301 --> 00:10:57.637
Ah, thank you very much.

00:10:57.637 --> 00:11:00.401
We're just getting started. Come on.

00:11:01.107 --> 00:11:04.076
Wow! You can drink like a fish, can't you?

00:11:06.012 --> 00:11:11.851
Ahh. People thought I was going to
be an executive at Galaxy Police,

00:11:11.851 --> 00:11:15.309
but now look what's happened to me!

00:11:28.201 --> 00:11:30.803
Please come and relax here.

00:11:30.803 --> 00:11:34.374
We have super beautiful girls.
You can't miss this chance!

00:11:34.374 --> 00:11:37.366
It's just like heaven,
only a little bit earlier!

00:11:46.586 --> 00:11:49.578
This is great, huh? Are we having fun, yet?

00:11:49.689 --> 00:11:51.824
Hi, how are you doing?

00:11:51.824 --> 00:11:53.416
- Nagi!
- Ah!

00:12:03.002 --> 00:12:04.970
What can I get for you?

00:12:06.072 --> 00:12:08.341
I'll have the "special of the house."

00:12:08.341 --> 00:12:10.206
Yes.

00:12:22.488 --> 00:12:24.319
Here you go.

00:12:32.498 --> 00:12:35.268
Hm. This is pretty good.

00:12:35.268 --> 00:12:37.668
Well, thank you very much.

00:12:39.305 --> 00:12:42.975
Tell me something. Seen this woman before?

00:12:42.975 --> 00:12:47.046
Let's see. Our place just opened here, so...

00:12:47.046 --> 00:12:48.741
So you haven't, huh?

00:12:51.384 --> 00:12:53.152
Thanks for the drink.

00:12:53.152 --> 00:12:55.254
This is your check, Ma'am.

00:12:55.254 --> 00:12:58.491
Hmm?

00:12:58.491 --> 00:13:00.860
Is this some kind of joke?!

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:02.595
Like I said, this is the bill.

00:13:02.595 --> 00:13:05.393
I just had one drink! You gotta be kidding!

00:13:09.268 --> 00:13:11.871
Thank you very much.

00:13:11.871 --> 00:13:13.706
Please come again.

00:13:13.706 --> 00:13:14.941
She seems to be very upset for some reason.

00:13:14.941 --> 00:13:16.943
I wonder what happened.

00:13:16.943 --> 00:13:18.478
You can dream on!

00:13:18.478 --> 00:13:24.144
- I'm never coming back!
Do you hear me? Never!
- Huh? What? Uh.

00:13:27.887 --> 00:13:30.256
1... 2... 3... 4...

00:13:30.256 --> 00:13:32.291
5... 6... 7...

00:13:32.291 --> 00:13:36.662
8... 9... 10...

00:13:36.662 --> 00:13:42.335
Being the Crown Princess as I am, why
do I have to be involved in this rip-off bar?

00:13:42.335 --> 00:13:46.005
Last I heard, you were a
fugitive in hiding. What can I say?

00:13:46.005 --> 00:13:48.074
Princess Ayeka, I am so sorry for you.

00:13:48.074 --> 00:13:51.511
Under different circumstances
you would be able to travel like royalty.

00:13:51.511 --> 00:13:58.474
Oh, I remember my first trip. Yes, I remember
my first trip to a neighboring galaxy.

00:14:06.459 --> 00:14:10.296
We visited famous places in the universe
full of natural beauty and historical interest.

00:14:10.296 --> 00:14:13.288
It really was a fabulous trip.

00:14:17.937 --> 00:14:23.136
Of course, we stayed in a
fancy hotel in the royal suite.

00:14:30.016 --> 00:14:32.678
Hmm? How strange.

00:14:37.723 --> 00:14:42.990
It should be a sweet memory, but
there seemed to be something unpleasant.

00:14:50.102 --> 00:14:52.036
Oh, now I know!

00:14:55.474 --> 00:14:58.739
Hey, there, you!
What are you doing on my bed?

00:15:03.282 --> 00:15:08.310
Nevertheless, the blue
ocean was still beautiful.

00:15:09.422 --> 00:15:11.982
Ahh, it is so calm and peaceful.

00:15:19.265 --> 00:15:21.062
Hey, you, get out of my way!

00:15:25.304 --> 00:15:28.507
You liar! You are just making up that story.

00:15:28.507 --> 00:15:30.676
Oh, I see. You're awake?

00:15:30.676 --> 00:15:35.170
What really happened was
I was working at a seaside hotel.

00:15:37.917 --> 00:15:40.152
You should feel honored
to be able to clean the room

00:15:40.152 --> 00:15:44.323
of the Crown Princess of Jurai's royal family.

00:15:44.323 --> 00:15:48.157
Yes, indeed. It's quite a privilege.

00:15:52.632 --> 00:15:58.004
But when I was out on
the ocean I felt so happy.

00:15:58.004 --> 00:15:59.904
It's so quiet.

00:16:01.007 --> 00:16:02.372
Huh?

00:16:06.979 --> 00:16:09.382
You are the biggest liar of all time!

00:16:09.382 --> 00:16:11.384
Takes one to know one, girl.

00:16:11.384 --> 00:16:13.953
Who do you think is telling the truth?

00:16:13.953 --> 00:16:16.956
Hmm. Both stories sound so real.

00:16:16.956 --> 00:16:19.892
Both of them must be telling the truth then.

00:16:19.892 --> 00:16:20.693
How rude!

00:16:20.693 --> 00:16:22.228
That's right!

00:16:22.228 --> 00:16:25.731
Well, I think I'm going to bed.

00:16:25.731 --> 00:16:27.133
Sasami, too.

00:16:27.133 --> 00:16:28.768
We should get some sleep, too.

00:16:28.768 --> 00:16:30.936
Yeah, 'cause we've got
to get up early tomorrow.

00:16:30.936 --> 00:16:33.769
We are off to bed, too.

00:16:36.375 --> 00:16:39.145
Oh, yeah. Did anyone
remember to turn off the gas?

00:16:39.145 --> 00:16:42.748
Yes, I remembered to do it!

00:16:42.748 --> 00:16:44.375
Oh, good.

00:16:48.421 --> 00:16:49.854
Heh?

00:16:55.795 --> 00:16:59.098
Headquarters to all patrol ships.
Headquarters to all patrol ships.

00:16:59.098 --> 00:17:02.868
There has just been a
mysterious explosion in zone 907.

00:17:02.868 --> 00:17:05.496
Proceed to the scene immediately. Repeat.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.985
We have discovered that
the explosion in zone 907

00:17:19.985 --> 00:17:22.355
was caused by Princess Ayeka and her group.

00:17:22.355 --> 00:17:24.346
All patrol ships, engage in pursuit.

00:17:29.295 --> 00:17:31.063
A whole bunch of 'em are coming after us.

00:17:31.063 --> 00:17:32.732
And it's all your fault, Mihoshi.

00:17:32.732 --> 00:17:34.500
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.468
Hurry. They're right behind us.

00:17:43.075 --> 00:17:44.810
Oh, no. A battleship of Jurai!

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.780
Battleships in front and
the Galaxy Police in back.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.577
What are we gonna do?

00:17:54.487 --> 00:17:55.888
It's Ken-Ohki.

00:17:55.888 --> 00:17:59.949
Oh, great! We have Nagi on our tail now, too?

00:18:02.094 --> 00:18:03.662
You cannot escape, Ryoko!

00:18:03.662 --> 00:18:05.857
I will defeat you!

00:18:19.478 --> 00:18:21.414
Ryoko is my prey!

00:18:21.414 --> 00:18:23.177
I won't let anybody interfere!

00:18:35.361 --> 00:18:36.896
While Nagi is distracted...

00:18:36.896 --> 00:18:38.864
Right! I know!

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.469
Huh? Ah! Stop!

00:18:43.469 --> 00:18:44.670
Where do you think you're going?

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.939
You take care of them for us, okay?

00:18:46.939 --> 00:18:48.930
What?!

00:18:49.675 --> 00:18:51.438
Hey. Hold on a minute!

00:18:59.652 --> 00:19:03.088
Damn you, Ryoko! Wait!

00:19:05.791 --> 00:19:09.895
Princess Ayeka is thought to be
responsible for the bombing on Planet Concor.

00:19:09.895 --> 00:19:12.731
The terrorist group exchanged fire with
the Galaxy Police patrol ships and fled...

00:19:12.731 --> 00:19:17.603
- Our station is continuing the search,
but so far we haven't found them.
- We are now terrorists, huh?

00:19:17.603 --> 00:19:22.341
Emperor Yosho delivered a
speech regarding this incident

00:19:22.341 --> 00:19:24.510
condemning it as a
rebellion against space peace.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.645
I don't know about this Yosho character.

00:19:26.645 --> 00:19:29.615
Can he really be that
legendary hero or I don't know.

00:19:29.615 --> 00:19:34.487
I think it's strange that he hasn't
appeared in front of the media yet.

00:19:34.487 --> 00:19:37.990
We have to reveal his
true identity or otherwise,

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.160
we will be wanted criminals forever, Tenchi.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.529
You think positive, Kiyone.

00:19:43.529 --> 00:19:47.266
Something will work out
once we get to Planet Jurai.

00:19:47.266 --> 00:19:51.635
But I really don't know whether or not
we'll ever make it to the Planet Jurai.

00:19:55.975 --> 00:19:59.712
<i>Photon, proton, synchrotron</i>

00:19:59.712 --> 00:20:03.682
<i>Science is far better than love can ever be</i>

00:20:03.682 --> 00:20:07.520
<i>Love relationships based
on the uncertainty principle</i>

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:11.891
<i>are really very stupid and boring</i>

00:20:11.891 --> 00:20:19.398
<i>As long as there is quantum mechanics</i>

00:20:19.398 --> 00:20:27.396
<i>We can break through
the wall of all dimensions</i>

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.384
Listen, through his thought experiments...

00:20:38.384 --> 00:20:41.053
Heisenberg concluded that the
product of the uncertainties of position

00:20:41.053 --> 00:20:43.956
and the uncertainties of momentum
is equal to or greater than h/2 pi,

00:20:43.956 --> 00:20:47.293
where "h" equals Planck's constant.

00:20:47.293 --> 00:20:49.094
It means that observations
in quantum mechanics

00:20:49.094 --> 00:20:52.264
always lead to uncertainty as to value.

00:20:52.264 --> 00:20:53.032
You understand this, don't you?

00:20:53.032 --> 00:20:54.863
Nope. Not at all.

00:20:55.301 --> 00:20:56.859
I think it's pretty hopeless.

00:22:55.554 --> 00:22:57.956
We're heading for Planet Jurai aboard Yagami.

00:22:57.956 --> 00:23:00.459
Yagami breaks down and we're
stalled in the middle of nowhere.

00:23:00.459 --> 00:23:03.529
Ryoko's gone on Ryo-Ohki for groceries.

00:23:03.529 --> 00:23:06.098
But will she come back
before we all starve to death?

00:23:06.098 --> 00:23:08.200
Aw! I'm so hungry!

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:12.805
Ryoko must have forgotten
about us having some fun by herself.

00:23:12.805 --> 00:23:14.339
We must trust her, everyone.

00:23:14.339 --> 00:23:17.042
If we believe, she will come back.

00:23:17.042 --> 00:23:19.144
What do you think this is, a fairy tale?!

00:23:19.144 --> 00:23:21.180
Next episode is: "No Need for Hunger!"

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:23.648
It's unquestionably disgraceful!
